### Scenarios for the class, in lesson order.
### Start the application first: ./mvnw spring-boot:run   (PostgreSQL starts from compose.yaml)
### Each request runs one scenario and returns its report as JSON; the SQL log shows the statements.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### List the scenarios
GET {{host}}/scenarios

### Shelf map — the persistence context (first-level cache)
POST {{host}}/scenarios/first-level-cache

### Catalogue — naive: 1 + 1 per author + 1 per book (look at the SQL log)
POST {{host}}/scenarios/catalogue-naive

### Catalogue — JOIN FETCH: one statement, entities still built
POST {{host}}/scenarios/catalogue-join-fetch

### Catalogue — projection: one statement, no entities
POST {{host}}/scenarios/catalogue-projection

### Catalogue endpoints (the response is the same for the three)
GET {{host}}/naive/books

###
GET {{host}}/naive/books?author=Prolific%20Author

###
GET {{host}}/better/books/join-fetch

###
GET {{host}}/better/books/projection

### Shelf map — naive: 2 statements, but 20,301 entities and one JSON object per copy
POST {{host}}/scenarios/shelf-map-naive

### Shelf map — projection and compact format
POST {{host}}/scenarios/shelf-map-projection

### Shelf map endpoints (branch by name: ids change at every start)
GET {{host}}/naive/branches/Central/shelf-map

###
GET {{host}}/better/branches/Central/shelf-map

### Unknown branch: 404 problem+json
GET {{host}}/better/branches/Nowhere/shelf-map

### Import — naive: 5,000 rows imported twice (about 40 s; the cost grows with the square of the rows)
# @timeout 300
POST {{host}}/scenarios/import-naive

### Import — batched: the same 5,000 rows, then 20,000
POST {{host}}/scenarios/import-batched

### Import endpoints: upload a file to Annex (re-uploading the same file updates, never duplicates)
POST {{host}}/better/branches/Annex/copies/import
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="annex-20000.csv"

< ./src/main/resources/import/annex-20000.csv
--boundary--

### An unknown ISBN on the last row: 400 with the line, and nothing imported.
### The naive version writes 4,999 copies before it finds it; the rollback undoes them.
POST {{host}}/naive/branches/Annex/copies/import
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="annex-5000-error-last-row.csv"

< ./src/main/resources/import/annex-5000-error-last-row.csv
--boundary--

### Reservation — naive: fifty members, one copy, all fifty told 201
POST {{host}}/scenarios/reservation-naive

### Reservation — pessimistic lock: one 201, forty-nine 409
POST {{host}}/scenarios/reservation-pessimistic

### Reservation — two overlapping requests, naive: the shared copy promised twice
POST {{host}}/scenarios/reservation-overlap-naive

### Reservation — two overlapping requests, with locks: the loser leaves no trace
POST {{host}}/scenarios/reservation-overlap-pessimistic

### Reserve a copy (business keys: ids change at every start). Run it twice: 201, then 409.
POST {{host}}/better/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"memberEmail": "member01@library.test", "branch": "North", "barcodes": ["N0010"]}

###
POST {{host}}/better/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"memberEmail": "member02@library.test", "branch": "North", "barcodes": ["N0010", "N0011"]}

### Member limit — copies locked, count unlocked: two tabs of one member end with 6 items (limit 5)
POST {{host}}/scenarios/member-limit-naive

### Member limit — member row locked first: one tab reserves, the other gets 409
POST {{host}}/scenarios/member-limit-locked

### Reserve with the member locked. Run after member-limit-locked (member53 then has 4 items): 409 member-limit-exceeded
POST {{host}}/better/reservations/member-locked
Content-Type: application/json

{"memberEmail": "member53@library.test", "branch": "North", "barcodes": ["N0025", "N0026", "N0027", "N0028"]}

### =============================================================================================
### Expiry, collection and return (design/reservation-expiry-and-return.md). Run with the scheduled
### sweep off (the default): the scenarios move the application's clock, 30 days into the past.
### =============================================================================================

### Expiry S1 — one operation at a time, 1 µs before the deadline and at it: all right, even naive
POST {{host}}/scenarios/expiry-boundary

### Expiry S2 — naive: collect and expire both succeed; the copy is in Anna's bag and on the shelf map
POST {{host}}/scenarios/collect-expiry-naive

### Expiry S2 — option A: member, reservation, copies locked; the clock read after the locks
POST {{host}}/scenarios/collect-expiry-locked

### Expiry S2 — option B: a conditional UPDATE on the reservation decides
POST {{host}}/scenarios/collect-expiry-conditional

### Expiry S3 — naive: a late cancel locks the row and still decides on the stale entity
POST {{host}}/scenarios/cancel-stale-naive

### Expiry S3 — better: scalar keys before the lock, the entity loaded under it: 409
POST {{host}}/scenarios/cancel-locked

### Expiry S4 — naive: the late sweep frees a copy Bruno reserved after the deadline
POST {{host}}/scenarios/sweep-after-rereserve-naive

### Expiry S4 — better: only the copies the reservation still holds are released
POST {{host}}/scenarios/sweep-after-rereserve-owned

### Expiry S5 — naive: the sweep locks in the opposite order: 40P01 deadlock (about 1 s per round)
POST {{host}}/scenarios/sweep-deadlock-naive

### Expiry S5 — better: one lock order everywhere, the sweep skips a busy member (SKIP LOCKED)
POST {{host}}/scenarios/sweep-ordered

### Expiry S6 — naive: two instances sweep the same 100 reservations: 200 notices
POST {{host}}/scenarios/sweep-two-workers-naive

### Expiry S6 — better: SKIP LOCKED, each reservation expired once, 100 notices
POST {{host}}/scenarios/sweep-two-workers-skip-locked

### Expiry S6b — naive: a notice sent, then the transaction rolls back
POST {{host}}/scenarios/expiry-notice-rollback-naive

### Expiry S6b — better: the notice is sent after the commit
POST {{host}}/scenarios/expiry-notice-after-commit

### Expiry S7 — naive: 1,000 expired reservations in one transaction (Bruno times out; one failure undoes all)
# @timeout 300
POST {{host}}/scenarios/sweep-one-transaction

### Expiry S7 — better: pages of 100, one transaction each (slower in total; nobody waits)
# @timeout 300
POST {{host}}/scenarios/sweep-batched

### Expiry S8 — naive: a retried return erases the reservation made in between
POST {{host}}/scenarios/return-double-scan-naive

### Expiry S8 — better: the loan row decides; the retry changes nothing
POST {{host}}/scenarios/return-conditional

### Expiry endpoints, live. 1. member03 reserves N0030 (keeps the id for the next requests)
POST {{host}}/better/reservations/member-locked
Content-Type: application/json

{"memberEmail": "member03@library.test", "branch": "North", "barcodes": ["N0030"]}

> {% client.global.set("reservationId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Read it: 200, ACTIVE
GET {{host}}/reservations/{{reservationId}}

### 3. Move the application's clock 48 hours forward
POST {{host}}/demo/clock?plusHours=48

### 4. Read it again: 410 Gone, although its row still says ACTIVE (lazy expiry on read)
GET {{host}}/reservations/{{reservationId}}

### 5. Collect it: 409 reservation-not-active
POST {{host}}/better/reservations/{{reservationId}}/collection
Content-Type: application/json

{"memberEmail": "member03@library.test"}

### 6. The clock back to the system clock
DELETE {{host}}/demo/clock

### 7. Collect it now: with the real clock back, its deadline is 48 h away again: 200 with the loan ids
POST {{host}}/better/reservations/{{reservationId}}/collection
Content-Type: application/json

{"memberEmail": "member03@library.test"}

> {% client.global.set("loanId", response.body.loanIds[0]); %}

### 8. Return the copy; run it twice: the retry answers 200 with the same loan
POST {{host}}/better/loans/{{loanId}}/return
